// REJECTS: Unexpected token ','
//
// business() milestoning is EITHER the snapshot form (BUS_SNAPSHOT_DATE) OR the range form
// (BUS_FROM/BUS_THRU). This asks for both in one entry. Unlike the auth case above, this
// one IS enforced by the grammar -- businessMilestoning has two disjoint alternatives -- so
// it fails at the comma rather than with a named-field message.
//
// The pair is deliberate: two mutual-exclusion rules, enforced at two different layers,
// producing two different diagnostics. A rewrite has to get both layers right.
###Relational
Database fixture::neg::BothMilestonings
(
   Table T
   (
      milestoning
      (
         business(BUS_SNAPSHOT_DATE = SNAP, BUS_FROM = FROM_Z, BUS_THRU = THRU_Z)
      )
      ID VARCHAR(32) PRIMARY KEY,
      SNAP DATE, FROM_Z DATE, THRU_Z DATE
   )
)
